## Getting Started

### Prerequisites

- Node.js 20+
- MongoDB running locally (or Atlas connection string)
- Supabase project (optional for sync features)

### 1. Clone the repository

```bash
git clone <repo-url>
cd sho-app
```

### 2. Start the backend

```bash
cd server
npm install
cp .env.example .env   # fill in your values (see below)
npm run dev            # node --watch server.js on port 5001
```

### 3. Start the frontend

```bash
cd app
npm install
npm run dev            # Vite dev server on port 3000
```

The Vite dev server proxies `/api/*` requests to `http://localhost:5001`, so no CORS configuration is needed during development.

### 4. Seed demo data (optional)

```bash
cd server
node seed-demo.js      # creates sample schools, batches, students, users
```

